{"dependencies":["Finset.sum_bij'","AddCommMonoid","Finset","Membership.mem","Finset.instMembership","Finset.sum","Eq"],"doc":"Reorder a sum.\n\nThe difference with `Finset.sum_nbij` is that the bijection is specified with an inverse, rather\nthan as a surjective injection.\n\nThe difference with `Finset.sum_bij'` is that the bijection and its inverse are non-dependent\nfunctions, rather than being allowed to use membership of the domains of the sums.\n\nThe difference with `Finset.sum_equiv` is that bijectivity is only required to hold on the domains\nof the sums, rather than on the entire types. ","extra":null,"kind":"theorem","levels":["u_1","u_2","u_3"],"module":"Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Defs","name":"Finset.sum_nbij'","nodes":[["sort",["succ",["param","u_1"]]],["sort",["succ",["param","u_2"]]],["sort",["succ",["param","u_3"]]],["constant","AddCommMonoid",[["param","u_3"]]],["bound",0],["apply",3,4],["constant","Finset",[["param","u_1"]]],["bound",3],["apply",6,7],["constant","Finset",[["param","u_2"]]],["apply",9,7],["bound",5],["bound",4],["forall","a._@._internal._hyg.0",11,12,"explicit"],["forall","a._@._internal._hyg.0",11,11,"explicit"],["bound",7],["forall","a._@._internal._hyg.0",15,15,"explicit"],["bound",9],["forall","a._@._internal._hyg.0",15,17,"explicit"],["constant","Membership.mem",[["param","u_1"],["param","u_1"]]],["bound",10],["apply",19,20],["apply",6,20],["apply",21,22],["constant","Finset.instMembership",[["param","u_1"]]],["apply",24,20],["apply",23,25],["bound",6],["apply",26,27],["apply",28,4],["constant","Membership.mem",[["param","u_2"],["param","u_2"]]],["apply",30,20],["apply",9,20],["apply",31,32],["constant","Finset.instMembership",[["param","u_2"]]],["apply",34,20],["apply",33,35],["apply",36,27],["bound",1],["apply",7,38],["apply",37,39],["forall","a._@._internal._hyg.0",29,40,"explicit"],["forall","a",17,41,"explicit"],["apply",37,4],["bound",12],["apply",19,44],["apply",6,44],["apply",45,46],["apply",24,44],["ap